wnload_count": 472, "created_at": "2026-10-14T08:37:12Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-14T08:37:13Z", "browser_download_url": "https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/releases/download/v265/llama-swap_265_linux_arm64.tar.gz"}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mostlygeek/llama-swap/releases/assets/639765290", "id": 639765290, "node_id": "RA_kwDOM7P8-M4mIgsq", "name": "llama-swap_265_windows_amd64.zip", "label": "", "uploader": {"login": "github-actions[bot]", "id": 41898282, "node_id": "MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D", "html_url": "https://github.com/apps/github-actions", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events", "type": "Bot", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "content_type": "application/zip", "state": "uploaded", "size": 23062503, "digest": "sha256:80b61f4e980a11e659d5c8973f8b72f22cc5f68eaa33e28645ff67c16763bcc9", "download_count": 1213, "created_at": "2026-10-14T08:37:14Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-14T08:37:15Z", "browser_download_url": "https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/releases/download/v265/llama-swap_265_windows_amd64.zip"}], "tarball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mostlygeek/llama-swap/tarball/v265", "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mostlygeek/llama-swap/zipball/v265", "body": "\nA couple of small improvements:\n\n- support serving llama-swap behind a path on a reverse proxy. Helpful if you want to front llama-swap with nginx and serve it under a specific path.\n- add support for manually defining voices for text to speech models\n- a small kubeswap update\n\n- [PR #1228](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1228) ui,server: serve the UI under a reverse proxy base path: makes the browser side base-path agnostic (relative asset, redirect, favicon and PWA URLs plus an `apiUrl()` helper that re-attaches a stripped prefix) so llama-swap works behind a plain prefix-stripping proxy at `https://host/subpath/llama-swap/` without routing `/ui`, `/api` and `/v1` at the proxy root; includes an nginx and Caddy guide (#1227) by [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)\n- [PR #1225](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1225) Add voices override for speech models: adds a `models.capabilities.voices` capability listing the voice ids an upstream server supports, because the non-standard `GET /v1/audio/voices` endpoint returns unreliable responses; falls back to probing that endpoint on a best-effort basis when the list is not set (#1207) by [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)\n- [PR #1224](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1224) cmd/kubeswap: attach DRA ResourceClaims and mount NFS volumes: adds a repeatable `--resource-claim name=claim` flag so backends can get GPUs via the NVIDIA DRA driver (kubeswap only references the claim, pods sharing a claim share its device) and an `nfs:server/export:path[:ro]` kind for `--volume` so models can be mounted from NFS without a static PV/PVC per export (#1222) by [@gabrielcosi](https://github.com/gabrielcosi)\n\n\n", "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mostlygeek/llama-swap/releases/412498540/reactions", "total_count": 8, "+1": 4, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 4, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}}